/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Component: the sodium salt of Bowen & Mohammad's trivalent dye -- CASE-
  LOCAL (nanofiltran03_bowen_mohammad_ca30).

  Bowen & Mohammad (AIChE J. 44 (1998) 1799) fed the CA30 membrane a
  reactive dye with sodium chloride; the dye anion is trivalent (Geraldes
  & Alves, J. Membr. Sci. 321 (2008) 172-182, section 4.1).  The DSPM-DE
  law decomposes a salt into its ions, so the dye enters this case as the
  salt that carries it, Na3Dye -> 3 Na+ + Dye3-; the feed's sodium is then
  the chloride's plus three per dye, which is the paper's electroneutral
  feed.  ONLY the ion stoichiometry the pore model reads, and no
  thermochemistry.  NEITHER PAPER STATES THE DYE'S MOLAR MASS: the `MW`
  below is NOT one -- the component grammar requires the key, and the
  props bench (feeds in mol/m3, permeates in mol/m3) converts no mass, so
  nothing reads it (the precedent: the NanoFiltran example membrane's A_w,
  carried because the record grammar requires one).  Do not copy it
  anywhere a mass is computed.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           Na3Dye;
MW             1000;            // NOT a molar mass: required by the grammar, read by nothing here

role           nonvolatile;
dissociation   4;               // van't Hoff factor
dissociatesTo  { Na 3; Dye 1; } // ion stoichiometry (formula-like identity)
